---
description: Hono on Bun — route modules, shared Zod, db package only
globs: apps/api/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# API (`apps/api`)

Bun-native server. Do not add Node, `@hono/node-server`, Express, or CORS.

```ts
// ✅ src/index.ts
app.route("/", healthRoutes);
app.route("/", authRoutes);
app.route("/", workspaceRoutes);
app.route("/", projectRoutes);
app.route("/", boardRoutes);
```

`src/index.ts` also exports `app` for tests (keep the Bun `export default`).

- One Hono app per route file (`new Hono()`), then `app.route("/", …)`.
- Product routes use `new Hono<SessionEnv>()` and `requireSession`
  (`src/middleware/session.ts`): `auth.api.getSession`, no session → 401
  `{ error }`, else `c.get("userId")`. Authorization order: session →
  membership (query in `@agentic-kanban/db`; missing or not a member → 404,
  never 403) → `workspace_id` from the DB row, never from body/query/params →
  every tenant query filters by it. Params use `@hono/zod-validator`.
- Build every response (including 401/404 `{ error }`) and pass it through
  `.parse()` of the shared schema before `c.json`; dates go out as ISO strings.
- Validate inputs (param/json via `zValidator` → 400) and responses with
  `@agentic-kanban/schemas`.
- `src/routes/board.ts` (`boardRoutes`): `GET /api/projects/:projectId/board`,
  `POST /api/projects/:projectId/tasks`, `PATCH`/`DELETE /api/tasks/:taskId`,
  `POST /api/tasks/:taskId/move` (`moveTaskBodySchema` → 200 task; the target
  column is validated against the task's own project, else 404).
  Data comes from the `*ForMember` queries in `@agentic-kanban/db`. Client ids
  only identify: `columnId` is validated against the authorized project (else
  404, no IDOR). `DELETE` answers 204 (`c.body(null, 204)`). Session 3 will
  publish realtime events from these write routes.
- Database access only through `@agentic-kanban/db`. Never import
  `@libsql/client` or `drizzle-orm` from the API.
- Better Auth (`src/auth/index.ts`, email/password, cookie session) is served
  by `src/routes/auth.ts` on `/api/auth/*` via `auth.handler(c.req.raw)`. Do
  not wrap those routes with `@hono/zod-validator`; Better Auth validates.
- `authRateLimit` (`src/auth/rate-limit.ts`): in-memory, 10/min per route on
  `POST` sign-up/sign-in, then 429. Off with `NODE_ENV=test` or
  `AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED=1`. `get-session` is never limited.
- `src/realtime/index.ts` stays a placeholder. Realtime must stay in this
  process (SSE or WebSocket). No Socket.IO, Redis, or extra service.
- Do not auto-run migrations or seed (apply with `docker compose exec api bun run db:migrate`, then `bun run db:seed`). Dev: `bun run --hot`. Listen
  `0.0.0.0:${API_PORT:-3000}`.
